---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '@/components/PageHero.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '@/components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import CTASection from '@/components/CTASection.astro';
import RelatedResources from '@/components/RelatedResources.astro';
import { CONTACT } from '@/lib/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Red Apple Export from Iran — Wholesale Iranian Red Apples | SibExport"
  description="Wholesale Iranian red apples for importers. SibExport supplies red apple export from Iran with defined grades, sizes and export packing. Request a quotation."
  path="/red-apple-export/"
  ogImage="/images/red-apple.png"
>
  <Breadcrumbs
    items={[
      { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
      { label: 'Iranian Apple Varieties', href: '/iranian-apple-varieties/' },
      { label: 'Red Apple Export' },
    ]}
  />
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Product"
    title="Red apple export from Iran"
    description="Colorful, crisp red apples sourced from Iranian orchards — sized, graded and packed to wholesale specification for international buyers."
  />

  <article class="container-site py-14 lg:py-20">
    <div class="prose-site mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <h2>Why red apples lead Iran's export program</h2>
      <p>
        Red apples are the backbone of Iran's fresh apple trade. The country
        is among the world's largest apple producers, and the cool-climate
        orchards of the northwest — particularly around Urmia in West
        Azerbaijan — produce red apples with the deep color, firm texture and
        balanced sugar content that wholesale buyers look for. For many
        importers in the region, Iranian red apples are a familiar, trusted
        category that moves steadily through wholesale and retail channels
        year after year.
      </p>
      <p>
        For a buyer, the commercial appeal is straightforward: strong visual
        appeal on the shelf, firmness that survives handling and long-distance
        transit, and a size range flexible enough to serve everything from
        family-pack retail programs to bulk wholesale markets. SibExport
        sources red apples from established growers in this region and
        prepares them for export against a written specification agreed with
        you before the order begins.
      </p>

      <h3>Characteristics buyers care about</h3>

    <figure class="my-8">
      <img
        src="/images/red-apple.svg"
        alt="Fresh red apples graded for export from Iran"
        width="1200"
        height="630"
        loading="lazy"
        class="w-full rounded-xl border border-border shadow-sm"
      />
      <figcaption class="mt-2 text-center text-xs text-muted-foreground">Fresh red apples graded for export from Iran</figcaption>
    </figure>
      <p>
        When importers evaluate red apple supply, a handful of characteristics
        decide whether the fruit performs in their market:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Color coverage</strong> — the depth and consistency of red
          blush across the fruit, which strongly influences retail presentation
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Firmness</strong> — the single best predictor of how well
          fruit survives transport and holds texture on arrival
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Size uniformity</strong> — a consistent count per carton
          that lets distributors plan predictable retail packs
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Sugar-acid balance</strong> — the eating profile customers
          expect from a good red apple: sweet, with enough acidity to taste
          fresh rather than flat
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Surface quality</strong> — freedom from blemishes, russeting
          and handling marks within the grade tolerance
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Iranian red apples perform well on all of these when they are
        harvested at the right maturity and handled correctly — which is
        exactly what our sourcing and inspection process is designed to
        ensure.
      </p>

      <h3>Varieties and availability</h3>
      <p>
        Iran's orchards include a range of commercially grown red apple
        varieties. Rather than promising a fixed variety list, we discuss
        availability with you against the season's actual crop: what is in
        harvest, what is in controlled-atmosphere or cold storage, and what
        genuinely matches the specification you need. This approach means the
        variety you confirm in your order is the variety that ships — not a
        brochure promise that quietly changes at packing time.
      </p>
      <blockquote>
        <strong>Note on accuracy:</strong> we do not publish variety claims we
        cannot confirm for a given season. Ask us what is currently available
        and we will answer with the facts.
      </blockquote>

      <h3>Size counts and grading for wholesale</h3>
      <p>
        Red apples for export are typically specified by <em>count per
        carton</em> — how many fruit fit a standard export carton — combined
        with a grade that sets tolerances for color, firmness and defects.
        Larger fruit means a lower count per carton; smaller fruit means
        higher counts. Your target market usually dictates the right
        combination: many retail programs favor mid-size fruit with strong
        color, while some wholesale markets prioritize larger, presentation
        fruit for loose display.
      </p>
      <p>
        Tell us the count and grade your market expects — or send a photo or
        specification sheet from your current supply — and we will match it
        from Iranian orchards. For a deeper explanation of how grading works,
        see our <a href="/apple-quality-specifications/">apple quality and
        specifications</a> page.
      </p>

      <h3>Packing and export preparation</h3>
      <p>
        Red apples ship in export-grade cartons with interior packaging that
        protects the fruit through transit. Standard configurations cover
        bulk wholesale cartons, and we can discuss retail-ready formats for
        supermarket programs. Carton dimensions, net weights, pallet
        configuration and labeling are all confirmed per order — details are
        covered on our <a href="/apple-packaging/">apple packaging</a> page.
      </p>
      <p>
        Because red apples are usually shipped to arrive with color and
        firmness intact, harvest timing, pre-cooling and cold-chain handling
        during loading matter as much as the packing itself. Our export
        preparation follows the same discipline described on the
        <a href="/apple-export-process/">export process</a> page.
      </p>

      <h3>Storage and transportation considerations</h3>
      <p>
        Fresh red apples are a living product: they continue to breathe after
        harvest, and their storage life depends on temperature management from
        the moment they are picked. Iranian export apples are typically held
        in cold storage to slow ripening and preserve firmness, and shipments
        are planned so transit time stays proportionate to the fruit's
        condition at dispatch.
      </p>
      <p>
        For regional destinations such as Iraq, the Gulf states or the
        Caucasus, road freight keeps transit times short — often a decisive
        advantage for fruit condition at arrival. We do not publish fixed
        shelf-life numbers, because honest figures depend on variety, harvest
        moment and storage history; ask us about the specific fruit you would
        be buying and we will give you a realistic picture.
      </p>

      <h3>Who this supply suits</h3>
      <p>
        Iranian red apples in wholesale volumes suit importers serving retail
        chains, wholesale produce markets, repackers and food distribution
        companies. Whether you buy a single truck load to test the market or
        plan a seasonal program across the harvest and storage months, the
        starting point is the same: send us your specification and destination,
        and we will respond with a realistic offer.
      </p>

      <h3>Commercial considerations for importers</h3>
      <p>
        Beyond fruit quality, several commercial factors shape a successful
        red apple import program. First, <strong>season positioning</strong>:
        fruit bought at harvest differs in price and behavior from fruit
        bought out of storage, and both have legitimate uses in a buying
        plan. Second, <strong>landed cost realism</strong>: the price per
        kilogram at origin is only one component of what fruit costs by the
        time it reaches your warehouse — packing density, pallet
        configuration and transport all move the final number. Third,
        <strong>supplier verification</strong>: before committing volume, ask
        exactly how fruit will be graded and who checks it; a supplier who
        answers in specifics is different from one who answers in adjectives.
      </p>
      <p>
        SibExport is structured for buyers who think this way. Our offers
        state the specification they are based on, our packing follows the
        agreed plan, and our inspection points exist so that questions are
        answered with evidence rather than reassurance.
      </p>

      <h3>What buyers typically require</h3>
      <p>
        Requirement profiles vary by market, but recurring themes include:
        consistent size counts across repeat orders; color standards
        appropriate to the destination's retail norms; cartons that present
        well on arrival rather than merely at departure; documentation
        matched to the importing country's phytosanitary rules; and
        communication that treats the buyer's schedule as binding. Where
        your requirement is unusual — a market-specific count, a proprietary
        label, an inspection protocol — put it in the inquiry. Unusual is
        normal in this trade; the point of the specification is to capture
        it.
      </p>

      <h3>The wholesale inquiry process</h3>
      <p>
        Working from inquiry to offer follows a short path. You send your
        requirement — via the <a href="/request-a-quotation/">quotation
        form</a>, WhatsApp or email. We confirm what the current season can
        supply against it and respond with a written offer: price, terms,
        packing, schedule. Questions are answered from the people handling
        the fruit, not a broker. Once terms are agreed, the order moves into
        sourcing, packing and loading under the process described on the
        <a href="/apple-export-process/">export process page</a>. First-time
        buyers usually find the clearest path is starting the conversation
        early — even weeks before a purchase decision — because seasonal
        availability rewards planning.
      </p>

      <h3>Frequently asked questions about red apple supply</h3>
      <p><strong>What sizes of red apples can I order?</strong><br />
      Size is specified as count per carton. Tell us your market's standard
      count — or the fruit size you currently buy — and we will confirm what
      Iranian supply can match this season.</p>
      <p><strong>Can I order retail-packed red apples?</strong><br />
      Retail-ready packing formats can be discussed as part of your
      quotation. Share your channel and target pack, and we will confirm
      options.</p>
      <p><strong>What is the minimum order quantity?</strong><br />
      MOQ depends on variety, packing and destination. Send your requirement
      and we will confirm the applicable minimum with your offer.</p>
      <p><strong>How do I get pricing?</strong><br />
      Pricing depends on variety, size, grade, volume, packing and delivery
      terms — which is why every quote is prepared per inquiry. Request a
      quotation and we will respond with a tailored offer.</p>
      <p><strong>Can I visit and inspect the fruit before shipment?</strong><br />
      Buyers are welcome to arrange inspection — including third-party
      inspectors — at agreed stages. Contact us to coordinate timing with
      your order.</p>
      <p><strong>Which destinations can red apples be shipped to?</strong><br />
      We are positioned for Iraq, the UAE, Russia, Armenia, Azerbaijan,
      Central Asia and other feasible markets. Current destination options
      are confirmed per order — see our <a href="/export-destinations/">export
      destinations</a> page for market notes.</p>
    </div>
  </article>

  <RelatedResources
    title="Regional apple trade resources"
    links={[
      {
        label: 'Urmia Apple Export and Wholesale',
        href: 'https://www.palude.ir/export/urmia-apple-export-wholesale/',
        description: 'Regional reference on apple export and wholesale supply from Urmia.',
      },
    ]}
  />

  <CTASection
    title="Ready to buy Iranian red apples in bulk?"
    description={`Send your sizes, grades, volume and destination — via the quotation form or WhatsApp at ${CONTACT.whatsappInternational} — and we will respond with a tailored offer.`}
  />
</BaseLayout>
